# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# .rooignore - keep the AI indexer / embedder OFF the huge + binary trees.
#
# WHY: Roo indexes the workspace with ollama embeddings (nomic-embed-text). That
# walk over model-training/ (41 GB) plus the model weight files is what pinned a
# CPU core at ~81 % and pushed the package to 75 C with fans at 4.5 k RPM.
#
# This is an EDITOR/AI scope only. Git tracking is unchanged and deliberate:
# models/fire/best.xml|best.bin|best.pt|labelmap.txt and models/coco/ ride the
# deploy via `git pull` (see .gitignore + dev_scripts/deploy_all.sh).
#
# The models/*.md provenance docs (README.md, VERSIONS.md) are intentionally NOT
# ignored, so the AI can still read model provenance.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Large local dataset / training trees (git-ignored, never shipped)
model-training/
fire-model-training/

# Generated model archives + fetched scene models
models/scene/
models/fire/versions/

# Opaque weight binaries (never useful to embed as text)
*.onnx
*.pt
*.bin

# Clip exports / media staging (huge, host-side artifacts)
firewatch_clips/
firewatch-fire-clips/
cam-clips/
camera-clips/
media/

# Training/eval output + caches
runs/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv*
